<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liugong Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liugong Island is a small island at the entrance to the harbour of Weihai in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It was the base of the Qing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beiyang-fleet">Beiyang Fleet</a>, which was destroyed there by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the Battle of Weihaiwei in 1895. Under the British lease of Weihaiwei from 1898 to 1930 it served as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> base and summer anchorage for the China Station.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liugong-island.jpg" alt="Liugong Island" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rolf Müller (Rolfmueller) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liugongisland_warmemorialhall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
